<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moran people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Moran are an indigenous people of upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a> in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, who once spoke a Bodo-Garo language now largely replaced by Assamese. They were among the first peoples absorbed into the Ahom kingdom after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukaphaa">Sukaphaa</a>'s arrival in the 13th century. Many later became disciples of the Moamara satra and formed the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moamoria-rebellion">Moamoria rebellion</a> that began in 1769.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moran-people.jpg" alt="Moran people" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jaideep kumar dohutia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moran_Bihu_Dance.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
